{
  "id": "mean-effect-size",
  "term": "mean effect size",
  "definition": "Mean effect size is the average magnitude of the effect being studied across the set of studies included in a meta-analysis. It is used to summarize the overall size of the investigated effect, distinct from heterogeneity, which reflects how consistent that effect is across studies.",
